zaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1ba506a15671a60d5cadb09dcf668d6c585b00030c6f2785b8bb736f393fdcbc","event_uuid":"4facd78e-9727-4db8-bb9c-47976454f59e","position":{"commit_sha":"bf3fc6ac916c150211a4c4198ce9dc60deb80910","position":"1788465363724523001-4facd78e-9727-4db8-bb9c-47976454f59e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788313898747264001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f654a20a-16a6-4edf-aa99-9104b0f5fee2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"887e-dc6c-0f5f-47b2"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:35-41,60-66,137-156` still honors `REBAR_HLC=0`, although `docs/remediation-implementation-plan.md:590-592` calls it a one-release rollback and many releases have since shipped. Disabling HLC can reintroduce causal-ordering errors under skewed clocks. The removal also affects compaction-concurrency scenarios that used the switch for timestamp placement and a seam guard that counts its `# read-via:` marker.\n\n## Approach\n\nRemove `_enabled`, the `REBAR_HLC` environment read, and the disabled raw-clock branch. Retain `REBAR_HLC_NOW` as the test-only physical-clock injection, legacy event reads, persisted-state locking, and deterministic clock tests. The generated environment reference must change through removal of the implementation read; no separate deprecation-registry entry exists to delete.\n\nMigrate the two compaction integration scenarios without disabling HLC. Scenario A will build its far-past subject from a fresh clone with no HLC cache, then use strictly ordered forward `REBAR_HLC_NOW` values for the young event, snapshot, and remote append; each tick is monotonic and the test proves the append sorts after the snapshot without a wall-clock race. Scenario B will create B’s below-snapshot orphan while B’s remote is disconnected and before B witnesses A’s future snapshot, using a valid injected future timestamp. After A publishes the higher future snapshot, reconnect B and drive a real engine write/push to merge and publish the pre-existing orphan; the test continues to prove detection and repair.\n\nUpdate all removal consumers: generated environment documentation, event-schema staging prose, the mechanism baseline, HLC unit tests, `test_store_paths` cleanup, the concurrency scenarios, and the held-out seam-marker budget. In the held-out guard, reduce both `_MARKER_BUDGET[\"_store/hlc.py\"]` from 2 to 1 and its exact-count `_TOTAL_MARKER_CAP` from 5 to 4, including the adjacent budget comment. Add a focused exact-name sweep/oracle so `REBAR_HLC` cannot reappear while the distinct `REBAR_HLC_NOW` injection remains allowed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- HLC implementation and generated environment reference\n- generated/operator and event-schema documentation plus the mechanism baseline\n- unit/store/integration/held-out consumers of the retired switch\n- a focused exact-name removal oracle\n\n## Testing\n\nRun the HLC unit suite, store-path test, both real push/fetch/merge compaction scenarios, the held-out snapshot-I/O seam guard, the environment-reference generator/check, lint, and typecheck. Use deterministic injected values and explicit cache/remote preconditions rather than wall-clock timing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The HLC implementation contains no `REBAR_HLC` disable branch or environment read; `REBAR_HLC_NOW` remains the sole test-time physical-clock override.\n- [x] Regenerating the environment reference after removing the implementation read produces no `REBAR_HLC=0` entry; `docs/event-schema.md` and completed-remediation guidance no longer describe it.\n- [x] `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` no longer contains the retired `env_var::REBAR_HLC` mechanism entry.\n- [x] Scenario A constructs its far-past ticket from a clone with an empty HLC cache and uses ordered forward injected clock values to prove the remote append sorts after the snapshot with HLC continuously enabled.\n- [x] Scenario B writes its below-snapshot orphan while disconnected before it can witness A’s higher snapshot, then reconnects through a real engine write/push and still proves orphan detection plus snapshot repair.\n- [x] In `tests/scripts/test_store_snapshot_io_seam_clean_heldout.py`, removal of the HLC read-via marker lowers `_MARKER_BUDGET[\"_store/hlc.py\"]` from 2 to 1, `_TOTAL_MARKER_CAP` from 5 to 4, and the associated budget comment so the exact-total guard remains valid.\n- [x] HLC unit and store-path tests preserve legacy event readability, injected-clock behavior, and canonical HLC-state placement without setting or clearing `REBAR_HLC`.\n- [x] A focused exact-name scan/test fails if `REBAR_HLC` is reintroduced outside the explicitly retained `REBAR_HLC_NOW` injection contract.\n- [x] The HLC, store, concurrency, seam-guard, environment-reference, lint, and typecheck suites pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/hlc.py","reason":"remove the expired disable branch while retaining HLC, state locking, and REBAR_HLC_NOW injection"},{"path":"src/rebar/_deprecations.py","reason":"remove any retired HLC environment registration"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"regenerated environment reference omits REBAR_HLC"},{"path":"docs/event-schema.md","reason":"remove staged rollback/disable prose"},{"path":"docs/remediation-implementation-plan.md","reason":"remove completed rollback-switch guidance"},{"path":".github/mechanism-baseline.json","reason":"remove retired env_var::REBAR_HLC mechanism baseline"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_hlc.py","reason":"retain always-HLC legacy-read and injected-clock coverage and add exact-name oracle"},{"path":"tests/unit/store/test_store_paths.py","reason":"remove obsolete REBAR_HLC fixture cleanup while preserving canonical state-path proof"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py","reason":"replace disable-switch timestamp placement with deterministic always-HLC offline/fresh-cache scenarios"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_store_snapshot_io_seam_clean_heldout.py","reason":"reduce retired HLC read-via marker budget from 2 to 1"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py","reason":"verify generated environment reference excludes the retired switch"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"],["relates_to","887e-dc6c-0f5f-47b2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"f5c4a7be-967c-4f44-8c8e-65399b8584b0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["janitor","store","deprecation","rp27"],"ticket_id":"fdd1-12fa-ce83-45d1","ticket_type":"story","title":"Retire the expired HLC rollback switch","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["dcbde3e5-9b7e-4db1-8a97-25c1b2197221","496dc160-cb30-4ce6-b75a-204bb342dfc0","2766639e-5c12-49e4-9a44-c3ddf8fbd41d","271d6a8a-08eb-4169-90c1-a75d57643a48","0aa53d78-91b3-4614-9cd8-95cfcceccbf1","8dee5962-56f1-4aba-9dc2-31b3e5374c5a","52159544-7e1c-43c2-9fb1-5ee380fc1d90","f654a20a-16a6-4edf-aa99-9104b0f5fee2","90395052-e0c4-4500-a35b-9dbf3fcd0849","43c86420-2db1-4cf6-8b5f-5b2047817826","f5c4a7be-967c-4f44-8c8e-65399b8584b0","4facd78e-9727-4db8-bb9c-47976454f59e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788472975994641001,"uuid":"daf76724-1d2c-44f6-a5f0-a6f58252dbda